## Still reproduces on 0.121.0 (latest)

Upgraded the consumer to Directive **0.121.0** (`npm i -g @deftai/directive@latest` + `directive update`; engine 0.121.0 = pin 0.121.0). The defect is unchanged.

**Source:** in `@deftai/directive-core@0.121.0` `dist/scope/acceptance-evidence.js`, `stampMatchAnyFileEvidence` still resolves the pointer with `resolveMatchAnyFilePointer` and writes `kind: "test"` without calling `evidencePointerShapeError`.

**Executable repro** against the installed 0.121.0 engine. A one-clause plan with `file_scope: ["docs/**"]` and `artifact_path: docs/guide.md`. Stamp it with the production writer, then run the same gate `scope:complete` uses:

```js
const m = await import('<global>/@deftai/directive-core/dist/scope/acceptance-evidence.js');
const plan = {
  id: 'repro', status: 'running',
  items: [{ id: 'clause.1', title: 'The guide documents the rule.', status: 'pending' }],
  acceptance: { commands: [], none_stated: true, source_rung: 'derived', ambiguity_attestation: 'none_found',
    clauses: [{ id: 1, text: 'The guide documents the rule.', artifact_path: 'docs/guide.md', ambiguous: false, provenance: 'statement' }] },
  metadata: { kind: 'story', swarm: { file_scope: ['docs/**'] } },
};
const stamp = m.stampMatchAnyFileEvidence(plan, { recorded_by: 'scope:stamp-evidence', projectRoot: root }); // root contains docs/guide.md
const ev = plan.items[0]['x-directive/evidence'];
m.evidencePointerShapeError(ev.kind, ev.pointer);
m.evaluateAcceptanceEvidenceGate(plan);
```

Output (Windows 11, Node 24.20.0):

```
directive-core 0.121.0
stamp result: {"stampedIds":["clause.1"],"skipped":[]}
stamped evidence: {"kind":"test","pointer":"docs/guide.md","recorded_at":"2026-10-05T16:56:29Z","recorded_by":"scope:stamp-evidence"}
evidencePointerShapeError: evidence kind mismatch: kind 'test' with a non-test artifact pointer — point at a test or declared code file, not markdown/CHANGELOG/PR prose (#5105)
gate ok: false
gate: {"ok":false,"message":"Acceptance evidence required for scope:complete (#3240 / #3305). 1 criterion/criteria missing suitable evidence or disposition:\n  - items[0] «untrusted:The guide documents the rule.»: evidence kind mismatch: kind 'test' with a non-test artifact pointer — point at a test or declared code file, not markdown/CHANGELOG/PR prose (#5105)\nEach non-terminal plan item needs x-directive/evidence {kind: test|review|merge|deploy|smoke|uat|observed_behavior, pointer, recorded_at, recorded_by} or x-directive/disposition {disposition: waived|deferred|not_applicable, reason, provenance {kind: operator-cli|operator-session|human-event, actor: <non-agent, e.g. operator@example.com>},
```

The production stamp writes a row (`stampedIds: ["clause.1"]`, no skip). The engine's own `evidencePointerShapeError` rejects that row, and `evaluateAcceptanceEvidenceGate` fails on it. Same result as on 0.119.12.
